FHE AI PRIVACY NOTES
Source: James Lockwood (@QBlazedog61029J)
→ 005.82 → Cryptography

CLAIM
  Barrier to enterprise AI = data privacy.
  Legal constraint: cannot send unencrypted customer data
  to third-party cloud ML models.
  Proposed fix: homomorphic evaluation so the model
  never sees plaintext.

CORE PROPERTY
  Enc(x)  +  Enc(y)  ->  Enc(x + y)
  Enc(x)  *  Enc(y)  ->  Enc(x * y)
  Decrypt(Eval(f, Enc(x))) = f(x)
  Server never holds sk.

SCHEME TYPES (OpenFHE)
  BFV   : exact integer arithmetic      (mod t)
  BGV   : exact integer arithmetic      (mod t, leveled)
  CKKS  : approximate real / complex    (SIMD slots)
  FHEW / TFHE / CGGI / DM / LMKCDEY
        : Boolean + LUT / functional bootstrap

TYPICAL OBJECTS / TYPES
  CryptoContext<DCRTPoly>   cc
  KeyPair                   kp = { pk, sk }
  PublicKey                 pk
  PrivateKey                sk
  Plaintext                 pt
  Ciphertext<DCRTPoly>      ct
  EvalKey                   relinKey, rotationKey, bootstrapKey

COMMON PARAMETERS / VARIABLES
  n, ringDim        ring dimension (power of 2)
  q, Q              ciphertext modulus (often CRT / DCRT)
  t, ptxtMod        plaintext modulus (BFV/BGV)
  scale, Delta      CKKS scaling factor
  L, multiplicativeDepth
  sigma             error / Gaussian noise stddev
  slots             packed SIMD lanes (CKKS / BFV)
  securityLevel     e.g. HEStd_128_classic
  batchSize         number of packed values
  firstModSize
  scalingModSize
  numLargeDigits    hybrid key-switch
  bootstrappingDepth / l_refresh

PIPELINE
  1. GenCryptoContext(params)
  2. KeyGen -> pk, sk
  3. EvalMultKeyGen / EvalRotateKeyGen / EvalBootstrapKeyGen
  4. Encode(x) -> pt
  5. Encrypt(pk, pt) -> ct
  6. EvalAdd / EvalSub / EvalMult / EvalRotate / EvalBootstrap
  7. Decrypt(sk, ct) -> pt' -> Decode

NOISE
  Every Mult (and some Add) grows noise.
  When noise approaches q/t (or scale budget in CKKS),
  bootstrap to refresh ciphertext.

RELATED FROM REPLIES
  Shamir Secret Sharing (threshold reconstruction):
    secret s split into shares s_i
    any t shares reconstruct s
    < t shares reveal nothing
  Complementary to FHE: split custody vs compute-on-ciphertext.

WHY IT MATTERS FOR HEALTHCARE / FINANCE
  PHI / PCI / PII stay encrypted in transit,
  at rest, AND during inference.
  Cloud sees only ct, never x.

LOCAL STACK MENTIONED IN THREAD CONTEXT
  OpenFHE (C++), often wrapped (Julia OpenFHE.jl, HEIR, etc.)
  High-spec laptop sufficient for prototype FHE, not yet
  for large production models without packing + hardware.
